n>• Defines security, testing, governance, compatibility, and documentation review priorities.\n>• Explicitly confirms no application behavior changes.\n></pre>\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Diagram</summary>\n\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n<br/>\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant A as Audit Request\n    participant B as Review Bots\n    participant R as Repository\n    A->>B: Trigger external review\n    B->>R: Inspect current main\n    R-->>B: Expose audit surfaces\n    B-->>A: Report findings\n```\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>High-Level Assessment</summary>\n\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n<br/>\n\n>The following are alternative approaches to this PR:\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>1. Use the PR description only</b></summary>\n\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n- ➕ Avoids retaining a dated audit artifact in the repository\n- ➕ Keeps review instructions attached to the relevant PR\n- ➖ May not satisfy bots that require a committed diff\n- ➖ Instructions become less discoverable after the PR closes\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>2. Add a manual audit workflow</b></summary>\n\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n- ➕ Provides a repeatable and explicit review trigger\n- ➕ Can standardize scope, permissions, and generated artifacts\n- ➖ Adds unnecessary automation and maintenance for a one-time audit\n- ➖ Requires careful permission and secret-boundary configuration\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n</details>\n\n>**Recommendation:** Keep the committed request file if external reviewers require an actual repository diff to run; it is the smallest behavior-neutral trigger. If bots can be invoked from PR text alone, prefer the PR description to avoid accumulating dated audit files.\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary> Files changed (1) <code> +14 / -0 </code> </summary>\n\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n<br/>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Documentation (1) <code> +14 / -0 </code></summary>\n\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n<details>\n<summary>CODE_REVIEW_AUDIT_2026-07-29.md<code>Define the external repository audit request</code> <code>+14/-0</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n>Define the external repository audit request\n>\n><pre>\n>• Adds a dated review request covering test validation, secret safety, Education gateway compatibility, governance consistency, pre-alpha safety boundaries, stale documentation, and architectural risks. It explicitly states that the audit branch does not intentionally alter application behavior.\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/SeCuReDmE-main-dev/fnpqnn_gateway_MVP/pull/6/files#diff-bee04d11f0a109d2cefd8e3fcdfc602ccf78a4d17d2e99e3609c9aba148a37e4'>.github/CODE_REVIEW_AUDIT_2026-07-29.md</a>\n\n</details>\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n</details>\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n</details>","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SeCuReDmE-main-dev/fnpqnn_gateway_MVP/issues/comments/5111445779/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":484649,"client_id":"Iv1.8b06d3cf5deea057","slug":"qodo-code-review","node_id":"A_kwHOCuzIt84AB2Up","owner":{"login":"qodo-ai","id":183290039,"node_id":"O_kgDOCuzItw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183290039?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/qodo-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":